[{:db/id 17592186195206 :answer-field/correct 17592186195210 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186195200 :answer-field/correct 17592186195202 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-181269"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070909/assets/f00499aad7b915267fe99bde8c13665a325cf6409e2e856466e9cdc90e4a8b8a.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,y\\,{{field-2}}\\,2x-3}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *below* the line $y=2x-3.$\n\nTherefore, a point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\ny<2x-3\n$$\n\nWe must also include the line $y=2x-3$ since the boundary is included in the set (the curve is solid). So, we change the inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\ny\\le 2x-3\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\le 2x-3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-181684/field-1/62fc74d0eb6ece7bf9beb52d92d3e5dd4c591eb0e1df3eb95bec90a49e0fa322" :answer/id #uuid "fd381acd-9dfb-5719-9dfb-397b55c60c9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{C}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181684/field-1/07d4d169afe54b72e6508fedd544e5d357fac0ff0f623249ab3b7f264f513fcf" :answer/id #uuid "79a183d8-de28-59a3-9974-d37d48fdd352" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181684/field-1/a1f44d584f3d5c0539cb338e6289ad49d176231f52c1da87f334282351fe2472" :answer/id #uuid "38ba16ce-61b2-57a5-929a-7e28ba89fffe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/i