:answer-field/id #uuid "2a378291-36f3-5534-9841-000847b38e3e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-182032/field-2/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" :answer-field/choices ["q-182032/field-2/55f4eef1ef55065220056c9644bf18d21761bc8db2d8f5c41f767a2fc9186b70" "q-182032/field-2/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" "q-182032/field-2/22814de28a0b1b4f20d5edd62707d192b78050d457a70349795d30d86dfcd7fa" "q-182032/field-2/cc57b3a2811193b1201e1d8d139011f0b8b63f9cad9aaf57f40ab2b8d40ee2eb" "q-182032/field-2/7d149b60a8e2a3be02476cb4e4d26616193c2006082edf79693d6816cf527c19"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-182032" :question/id #uuid "71c1be23-98af-5443-8ca0-30e1ee2b6297" :question/math-academy-id "q-182032" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070909/assets/980ae73286ed41ed0c6f074a4bed5b35fa852dd608fb0a1a561f26a7eac60ea7.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,x\\,{{field-2}}\\,2}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since all points $P(x,y)$ in our set lie at integer values of $x$ and $y,$ we have $x\\in Z,y\\in Z,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe points in our set include all those that lie *to the left* the line $x=2.$ For those points, the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\nx<2\n$$\n\nSince the boundary is *not* included in the set (the curve is *not* solid),  no further action must be taken, so we have\n\n$$\nx<2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,x<2}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-182032/field-1" "q-182032/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e694b201-5ec6-5cc3-a608-2447d1cc1ed3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-182032"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
